================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

The Windows .exe and the Android APK bundle the following open-source
components. The LICENSES/ directory of the source repository contains the
LGPL-3.0/GPL-3.0 texts (huawei-lte-api), the DejaVu font license and the
license and notice texts of the Python packages pinned in requirements.txt
(LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt); these files are attached to every
release and included in the APK. The other components listed below (native
runtimes and the Android build dependencies) are distributed under the
licenses named for them; their full texts are published by the respective
projects.

* huawei-lte-api — https://github.com/Salamek/huawei-lte-api
  Copyright (c) Adam Schubert (Salamek) and contributors.
  Licensed under LGPL-3.0 (LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt, which refers to
  LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt). Used unmodified as a separate library; its source
  code is available at the URL above and on PyPI. Performs all low-level
  communication with the Huawei router web API.

* requests (Apache-2.0), urllib3 (MIT), idna (BSD-3-Clause),
  charset-normalizer (MIT), certifi (MPL-2.0, source on PyPI),
  xmltodict (MIT), pycryptodome / pycryptodomex (BSD-2-Clause and public
  domain) — dependencies of huawei-lte-api.

* Python (PSF License), Tcl/Tk (Tcl license), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0),
  libffi (MIT), zlib (zlib), expat (MIT), bzip2 (bzip2 license),
  xz/liblzma (public domain) — Windows version runtime, packaged with
  PyInstaller (bootloader: GPL-2.0 with an exception that permits
  distributing packaged applications under any license).

* Python (PSF License), Kivy (MIT), python-for-android (MIT),
  pyjnius (MIT), SDL2 and its companion libraries (zlib), OpenSSL
  (Apache-2.0) — Android version runtime. The python-for-android recipes
  also add pycryptodome (instead of pycryptodomex), cffi (MIT), pycparser
  (BSD-3-Clause), setuptools (MIT), six (MIT), SQLite (public domain) and
  chardet (license of the version installed by the Kivy recipe, published
  by the chardet project).

* DejaVu Sans and DejaVu Sans Bold fonts (assets/DejaVuSans.ttf,
  assets/DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf, Android version, unmodified) — Bitstream Vera
  derived license, see LICENSES/DejaVu-Fonts.txt.
